\title{RAILS: Raking with Assisted Nested Propensity Score and LIFO Selection}
\description{
Combines a non-probability sample (e.g. a volunteer biobank) with a probability reference sample to produce population-representative weights. The core estimator fits a pseudo-likelihood propensity model on all interactions up to a base order, selects higher-order interactions by a forward likelihood-ratio test, and applies last-in-first-out stepwise raking to reference population margins. All computation runs on aggregated covariate cells. Variance is available from a stacked estimating-equation sandwich that accounts for uncertainty in the estimated weights, and a subgroup wrapper runs the procedure within levels of a stratifying variable.
